    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $P$ be the probability that Alice wins. Alice wins immediately with probability $1/2$. If she gets tails (probability $1/2$), Bob gets a turn. Bob wins with probability $1/2$ (tails), so Alice loses in this branch with probability $(1/2)(1/2) = 1/4$. If Bob also fails to win (gets heads, probability $1/2$), the turn returns to Alice, and the situation resets, meaning Alice has probability $P$ of winning from that point. Thus, $P = 1/2 + (1/2)(1/2)P = 1/2 + P/4$. Solving for $P$, we get $3P/4 = 1/2$, which yields $P = 2/3$.\n\n\\boxed{2/3}",
