    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To ensure all three lanes are occupied, we must distribute 6 distinct cars into 3 distinct non-empty lanes. This is equivalent to finding the number of surjective functions from a set of 6 elements to a set of 3 elements, which is calculated using Stirling numbers of the second kind multiplied by $3!$. The number of ways is $3! \\times S(6,3) = 6 \\times 90 = 540$.\n\n\\boxed{540}",
