      "generated_answer": "From the first equation, $\\log_6((x-y)(x+y)) = 2$ implies $x^2 - y^2 = 36$. From the second equation, $\\log_y(5x) = 2$ implies $y^2 = 5x$. Substituting $y^2 = 5x$ into the first equation gives $x^2 - 5x - 36 = 0$, which factors to $(x-9)(x+4) = 0$. Since $x$ must be positive for the logarithms to be defined in the context of real numbers (specifically $5x > 0$ and base $y > 0, y \\neq 1$), we discard $x = -4$. Thus, $x = 9$.\n\n\\boxed{9}",
