    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability of getting exactly three heads in five flips of a balanced coin, we use the binomial probability formula $P(X=k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}$. With $n=5$, $k=3$, and $p=0.5$, the calculation is $\\binom{5}{3} (0.5)^3 (0.5)^2 = 10 \\times 0.03125 = 0.3125$. Converting this to a percentage gives $31.25\\%$.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
