    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the limit of $\\frac{a_1 + 2a_2 + \\dots + n a_n}{n^2}$ given that $\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} a_n = 1$, we can use the Stolz-Cesàro theorem. Let $x_n = \\sum_{k=1}^n k a_k$ and $y_n = n^2$. Since $y_n$ is strictly increasing and divergent, the limit is equal to $\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{x_n - x_{n-1}}{y_n - y_{n-1}} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{n a_n}{n^2 - (n-1)^2} = \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{n a_n}{2n - 1}$. As $n \\to \\infty$, this simplifies to $\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{a_n}{2 - 1/n} = \\frac{1}{2}$.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
