      "generated_answer": "To determine the maximum number of acute angles in a convex $n$-gon, we consider the sum of exterior angles. The sum of the exterior angles of any convex polygon is $360^\\circ$. An interior angle is acute if it is less than $90^\\circ$, which means its corresponding exterior angle is greater than $90^\\circ$. Since each exterior angle must be positive and less than $180^\\circ$ for a strictly convex polygon, at most three exterior angles can exceed $90^\\circ$ (because $4 \\times 90^\\circ = 360^\\circ$, so four angles strictly greater than $90^\\circ$ would sum to more than $360^\\circ$). Therefore, there can be at most 3 acute interior angles.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
