      "generated_answer": "Let $g(x) = ax^6 - bx^4 + x$. Then $f(x) = g(x) - 1$. Given $f(2) = 5$, we have $g(2) - 1 = 5$, so $g(2) = 6$. Since $g(x)$ contains even powers of $x$ except for the linear term, let $h(x) = ax^6 - bx^4$, which is an even function ($h(-x)=h(x)$). Thus $g(-2) = h(-2) + (-2) = h(2) - 2$. We know $g(2) = h(2) + 2 = 6$, so $h(2) = 4$. Therefore, $g(-2) = 4 - 2 = 2$. Finally, $f(-2) = g(-2) - 1 = 2 - 1 = 1$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
