      "generated_answer": "\nThe condition that $x-3$ and $y+3$ are multiples of 7 implies $x \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}$ and $y \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$. Substituting these into $x^2 + xy + y^2$ gives $x^2 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$, $xy \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7}$, and $y^2 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$, so $x^2 + xy + y^2 \\equiv 2 + 5 + 2 \\equiv 9 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$. To make $x^2 + xy + y^2 + n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7}$, $n \\equiv -2 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7}$. The smallest positive integer $n$ satisfying this is 5, which corresponds to option C.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{C}}",
