      "generated_answer": "The vector space $V$ consists of $2 \\times 3$ matrices, so its dimension is $2 \\times 3 = 6$. The vector space $W$ consists of $4 \\times 1$ column vectors, so its dimension is $4$. Since $T$ is a linear transformation from $V$ onto $W$, the image of $T$ is $W$, meaning the rank of $T$ is $\\dim(W) = 4$. By the Rank-Nullity Theorem, $\\dim(\\ker(T)) = \\dim(V) - \\text{rank}(T) = 6 - 4 = 2$.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
