      "generated_answer": "The product of the numbers rolled will be composite unless it is prime or 1. Since the minimum value on a die is 1, the only way to get a non-composite result (1 or prime) is if the product is 1 (all dice show 1) or if the product is a prime number. A product of dice faces can only be prime if four dice show 1 and one die shows a prime number (2, 3, or 5). There are $1 + 3 \\times 5 = 16$ such outcomes out of $6^5 = 7776$. Thus, the probability of getting a composite number is $1 - \\frac{16}{7776} = \\frac{7760}{7776}$, which simplifies to $\\frac{485}{486}$.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
