    "global index": "MathQA_1373",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: the average expenditure of a labourer for 10 months was 85 and he fell into debt . in the next 4 months by reducing his monthly expenses to 60 he not only cleared off his debt but also saved 30 . his monthly income is\n\nOptions: \nA. 180\nB. 100\nC. 112\nD. 110\nE. none of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, calculate the total expenditure over the year: $85 \\times 10 = 850$ for the first 10 months and $60 \\times 4 = 240$ for the next 4 months, totaling $1090$. The laborer cleared his debt and saved 30, meaning his total income exceeded his total expenditure by 30. Therefore, total income is $1090 + 30 = 1120$, and the monthly income is $1120 / 12 = 93.33$, which does not match options A-D. However, re-reading the problem implies \"saved 30\" might refer to net position relative to debt clearance. Let's assume Income $I$. Total Income $= 12I$. Total Expenditure $= 1090$. Net $= 12I - 1090$. The problem states he cleared debt and saved 30. This usually means $(Total Income) - (Total Expenditure) = Savings - Debt_{initial}$. Or simpler: He had a debt $D$ after 10 months. Expenditure was $850$, Income $10I$. So $D = 850 - 10I$. In next 4 months, he earns $4I$ and spends $240$. He pays off $D$ and has 30 left. So $4I - 240 = D + 30$. Substitute $D$: $4I - 240 = (850 - 10I) + 30 \\Rightarrow 14I = 1120 \\Rightarrow I = 80$. Wait, let me re-calculate. $4I - 240 = 880 - 10I \\Rightarrow 14I = 1120 \\Rightarrow I = 80$. 80 is not in the options. Let me check option E.\n\nLet's re-read carefully. \"Average expenditure... 85\". Total exp 10 months = 850. \"Reducing monthly expenses to 60\". Total exp 4 months = 240. Total exp year = 1090. \"Cleared off his debt but also saved 30\". This implies Total Income - Total Expenditure = 30? No, because there was prior debt.\nLet Monthly Income be $x$.\nIncome for 10 months = $10x$. Expenditure = 850. Debt accumulated = $850 - 10x$.\nIncome for next 4 months = $4x$. Expenditure = 240.\nSurplus from last 4 months = $4x - 240$.\nThis surplus clears the debt ($850 - 10x$) and leaves 30.\nSo, $4x - 240 = (850 - 10x) + 30$.\n$14x = 1120$.\n$x = 80$.\n\nThe calculated monthly income is 80. This is not among options A, B, C, or D.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 402,
        "output_tokens": 711,
        "total_tokens": 1113
      },
      "provider": "agnes",
