      "generated_answer": "\nThe minimum bit time is 1 μs, so the bit rate must be at least 1 Mbps. With a voice bandwidth of 3 kHz, the Nyquist sampling rate is 6 kHz, and with a quantization level of 16 (4 bits per sample), the bit rate per signal is 24 kbps. For n signals, the total bit rate is n × 24 kbps. Setting n × 24,000 ≥ 1,000,000 gives n ≥ 41.67. The closest option satisfying n ≥ 41.67 is 45 signals, as it ensures the bit time is less than 1 μs.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{A}}",
