    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If 4 cards are drawn at random and without replacement from a deck of 52 playing cards, what is the chance of drawing the 4 aces as the first 4 cards?\n\nOptions: \nA. .000057\nB. .000037\nC. .000107\nD. .000077\nE. .000007\nF. .000097\nG. .000027\nH. .000047\nI. .000017\nJ. .000002\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We need the probability that the first 4 cards drawn are all aces.\n\nThe probability is:\n(4/52) × (3/51) × (2/50) × (1/49)\n\n= 24/(52 × 51 × 50 × 49)\n= 24/6,497,400\n≈ 0.00000369\n\nLet me compute more precisely:\n52 × 51 = 2652\n2652 × 50 = 132,600\n132,600 × 49 = 6,497,400\n24/6,497,400 ≈ 0.000003694\n\nThis is approximately 0.0000037, which matches option B (0.000037).\n\nWait, let me recheck: 24/6,497,400 = 0.000003694, which rounds to 0.000004, not 0.000037.\n\nLet me recompute: 0.000003694... Hmm, this is closer to 0.000004. None of the options match exactly, but B = 0.000037 is the closest. Actually, let me verify: 1/6,497,400 ≈ 1.539 × 10⁻⁷, so 24/6,497,400 ≈ 3.69 × 10⁻⁶ = 0.00000369.\n\nThe closest answer is B (0.000037), but there's a factor of 10 discrepancy. However, among the given choices, B is the intended answer since it's the only one in the right order of magnitude range (3.7 × 10⁻⁵ vs 3.7 × 10⁻⁶).\n\n\\boxed{B}",
