      "generated_answer": "To find the Fourier cosine series of $f(x) = x$ on $(0, c)$, we calculate the coefficients $a_0$ and $a_n$. The constant term is $a_0/2 = \\frac{1}{c} \\int_0^c x dx = c/2$. For $n \\ge 1$, $a_n = \\frac{2}{c} \\int_0^c x \\cos(\\frac{n\\pi x}{c}) dx$. Integration by parts yields $a_n = \\frac{2c}{n^2\\pi^2}[(-1)^n - 1]$. This is zero for even $n$ and $-4c/(n^2\\pi^2)$ for odd $n$. Thus, the series is $\\frac{c}{2} - \\frac{4c}{\\pi^2} \\sum_{k=0}^\\infty \\frac{\\cos((2k+1)\\pi x/c)}{(2k+1)^2}$, which matches option D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
