    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10946",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The cost of making the correct decisions for the given binary channel is zero, i.e., c(d_1/x_1) = c(d_2/x_2) = 0. The cost of making the incorrect decision d_1 is twice as much as that of making the incorrect decision d_2. That is to say, c(d_1/x_2) = 2c(d_2/x_1) which decision should be made, first, (a) When a y_1 is received, and (b) When a y_2 is received? GivenP(y_1/x_1) = 0.8, P(y_2/x_2) = 0.6, andP(x_1) = 0.8\n\nOptions: \nA. (a) Decision made is d_1, (b) Decision d_1\nB. (a) Decision made is d_2, (b) Decision d_2\nC. (a) Decision made is random, (b) No decision is made\nD. (a) Decision made is d_2, (b) Decision d_1\nE. (a) Decision made is d_1, (b) No decision is made\nF. (a) No decision is made, (b) Decision made is d_2\nG. (a) No decision is made, (b) Decision made is d_1\nH. (a) Decision made is d_1, (b) Decision d_2\nI. (a) Decision made is random between d_1 and d_2, (b) Decision d_1\nJ. (a) Decision made is d_2, (b) Decision is random between d_1 and d_2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the optimal decision rule, we calculate the posterior probabilities $P(x_i|y_j)$ and compare the expected costs (risk) for each decision $d_1$ (decide $x_1$) and $d_2$ (decide $x_2$).\n\nGiven:\n$P(x_1) = 0.8$, so $P(x_2) = 0.2$.\n$P(y_1|x_1) = 0.8$, so $P(y_2|x_1) = 0.2$.\n$P(y_2|x_2) = 0.6$, so $P(y_1|x_2) = 0.4$.\n\nCosts:\n$c(d_1|x_1) = 0$\n$c(d_2|x_2) = 0$\n$c(d_1|x_2) = C$\n$c(d_2|x_1) = 2C$\n(where $C > 0$).\n\n**Case (a): Received $y_1$**\nFirst, find $P(y_1)$:\n$P(y_1) = P(y_1|x_1)P(x_1) + P(y_1|x_2)P(x_2) = 0.8(0.8) + 0.4(0.2) = 0.64 + 0.08 = 0.72$.\n\nPosterior probabilities:\n$P(x_1|y_1) = \\frac{P(y_1|x_1)P(x_1)}{P(y_1)} = \\frac{0.64}{0.72} = \\frac{8}{9}$.\n$P(x_2|y_1) = \\frac{P(y_1|x_2)P(x_2)}{P(y_1)} = \\frac{0.08}{0.72} = \\frac{1}{9}$.\n\nExpected Costs:\nRisk($d_1$) = $c(d_1|x_1)P(x_1|y_1) + c(d_1|x_2)P(x_2|y_1) = 0 \\cdot \\frac{8}{9} + C \\cdot \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{C}{9}$.\nRisk($d_2$) = $c(d_2|x_1)P(x_1|y_1) + c(d_2|x_2)P(x_2|y_1) = 2C \\cdot \\frac{8}{9} + 0 \\cdot \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{16C}{9}$.\n\nSince $\\frac{C}{9} < \\frac{16C}{9}$, choose **$d_1$**.\n\n**Case (b): Received $y_2$**\nFirst, find $P(y_2)$:\n$P(y_2) = P(y_2|x_1)P(x_1) + P(y_2|x_2)P(x_2) = 0.2(0.8) + 0.6(0.2) = 0.16 + 0.12 = 0.28$.\n\nPosterior probabilities:\n$P(x_1|y_2) = \\frac{P(y_2|x_1)P(x_1)}{P(y_2)} = \\frac{0.16}{0.28} = \\frac{4}{7}$.\n$P(x_2|y_2) = \\frac{P(y_2|x_2)P(x_2)}{P(y_2)} = \\frac{0.12}{0.28} = \\frac{3}{7}$.\n\nExpected Costs:\nRisk($d_1$) = $c(d_1|x_1)P(x_1|y_2) + c(d_1|x_2)P(x_2|y_2) = 0 \\cdot \\frac{4}{7} + C \\cdot \\frac{3}{7} = \\frac{3C}{7}$.\nRisk($d_2$) = $c(d_2|x_1)P(x_1|y_2) + c(d_2|x_2)P(x_2|y_2) = 2C \\cdot \\frac{4}{7} + 0 \\cdot \\frac{3}{7} = \\frac{8C}{7}$.\n\nSince $\\frac{3C}{7} < \\frac{8C}{7}$, choose **$d_1$**.\n\nThus, the decisions are (a) $d_1$ and (b) $d_1$. This corresponds to Option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 682,
        "output_tokens": 1068,
        "total_tokens": 1750
      },
      "provider": "agnes",
