    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the convergence of $G(s) = \\int_0^\\infty e^{-st} dt$, we evaluate the integral as $\\lim_{T \\to \\infty} \\left[ -\\frac{1}{s} e^{-st} \\right]_0^T = \\frac{1}{s}$. This limit exists and equals $\\frac{1}{s}$ if and only if the real part of $s$ is positive ($\\text{Re}(s) > 0$), ensuring the exponential term decays. Therefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)=1$ is $1/s$ for $\\text{Re}(s) > 0$.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
