    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10311",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate f(t) if F(s) = [(3s^2 + 17s + 47) / {{(s + 2)(s^2 + 4s + 29)}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. f(t) = [e^-2t + 2.24e^-2tsin(5t - 26.6°)] u(t)\nB. f(t) = [e^-2t + 2.24e^-2tcos(5t - 26.6°)] u(t)\nC. f(t) = [e^-2t - 2.24e^-2tcos(5t - 26.6°)] u(t)\nD. f(t) = [e^-2t + 2.24e^-2tcos(5t + 26.6°)] u(t)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the inverse Laplace transform of F(s) = (3s² + 17s + 47)/[(s+2)(s² + 4s + 29)].\n\n**Partial Fraction Decomposition:**\n$$\\frac{3s^2+17s+47}{(s+2)(s^2+4s+29)} = \\frac{A}{s+2} + \\frac{Bs+C}{s^2+4s+29}$$\n\nSetting s = -2: A = (12-34+47)/25 = 1\n\nEquating numerators: 3s² + 17s + 47 = (s² + 4s + 29) + (Bs+C)(s+2)\n- Coefficient of s²: B = 2\n- Coefficient of s: 2B + C = 13, so C = 9\n- Constant: 2C = 18, but 29 + 18 = 47 ✓\n\n**Complete the square:** s² + 4s + 29 = (s+2)² + 25\n\n$$F(s) = \\frac{1}{s+2} + \\frac{2(s+2)}{(s+2)^2+25} + \\frac{5}{(s+2)^2+25}$$\n\n**Inverse Laplace Transform:**\n- First term: e^(-2t)\n- Second term: 2e^(-2t)cos(5t)\n- Third term: e^(-2t)sin(5t)\n\n**Combining sine and cosine:**\n$$2e^{-2t}\\cos(5t) + e^{-2t}\\sin(5t) = e^{-2t}[2\\cos(5t) + \\sin(5t)]$$\n\nConverting to single sinusoid: 2cos(5t) + sin(5t) = R·cos(5t - φ)\n- R = √(4+1) = √5 ≈ 2.236\n- φ = arctan(1/2) ≈ 26.57°\n\nTherefore: f(t) = [e^(-2t) + 2.24e^(-2t)cos(5t - 26.6°)]u(t)\n\n\\boxed{B}",
