    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\nThe correct solution is found by summing the steady-state and homogeneous solutions. The homogeneous equation \\(y[n] - \\frac{5}{6}y[n-1] + \\frac{1}{6}y[n-2] = 0\\) has characteristic roots \\(r = \\frac{1}{3}\\) and \\(r = \\frac{1}{2}\\), giving the homogeneous solution \\(y_h[n] = A \\cdot (\\frac{1}{3})^n + B \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})^n\\). The steady-state solution for the constant input \\(= 2\\) is \\(y_p[n] = 6\\). Using initial conditions \\(y[-1] = 1\\) and \\(y[-2] = -7\\), the constants are \\(A = -1\\) and \\(B = -1\\), yielding \\(y[n] = 6 - (\\frac{1}{2})^n - (\\frac{1}{3})^n\\), which matches option B.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{B}}",
