    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The vector field is radial, $\\mathbf{F} = k r^n \\hat{\\mathbf{r}}$. On the surface of the sphere $S$ with radius $a$, the normal vector is $\\hat{\\mathbf{n}} = \\hat{\\mathbf{r}}$.\n\nFirst, evaluate the flux integral $\\iint_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\hat{\\mathbf{n}} \\, dS$:\n$$ \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\hat{\\mathbf{n}} = (k a^n \\hat{\\mathbf{r}}) \\cdot \\hat{\\mathbf{r}} = k a^n $$\nSince this is constant over the sphere's surface, the integral becomes:\n$$ \\iint_S k a^n \\, dS = k a^n \\iint_S dS = k a^n (4 \\pi a^2) = 4 \\pi k a^{n+2} $$\n\nNext, evaluate the vector surface integral $\\iint_S \\mathbf{F} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{n}} \\, dS$:\n$$ \\mathbf{F} \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{n}} = (k a^n \\hat{\\mathbf{r}}) \\times \\hat{\\mathbf{r}} = \\mathbf{0} $$\nThus, the integral is zero.\n\nComparing the results $(4 \\pi k a^{n+2}, 0)$ with the options:\nA. $2\\pi k a^{n+3}, -1$\nB. $4\\pi k a^{n+2}, 0$\nC. $2\\pi k a^{n+2}, 0$\nD. $6\\pi k a^{n+2}, \\pi$\n...\n\nOption B matches our calculated values.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
