      "generated_answer": "To find the convolution $f(t) * g(t)$ for causal signals starting at $t=0$, we use the definition:\n$$ (f * g)(t) = \\int_0^t f(\\tau) g(t-\\tau) d\\tau $$\nSubstituting $f(\\tau) = \\tau$ and $g(t-\\tau) = (t-\\tau)^2$:\n$$ \\int_0^t \\tau (t-\\tau)^2 d\\tau = \\int_0^t \\tau (t^2 - 2t\\tau + \\tau^2) d\\tau = \\int_0^t (t^2\\tau - 2t\\tau^2 + \\tau^3) d\\tau $$\nEvaluating the integral:\n$$ \\left[ \\frac{t^2\\tau^2}{2} - \\frac{2t\\tau^3}{3} + \\frac{\\tau^4}{4} \\right]_0^t = \\frac{t^4}{2} - \\frac{2t^4}{3} + \\frac{t^4}{4} $$\nFinding a common denominator (12):\n$$ \\frac{6t^4}{12} - \\frac{8t^4}{12} + \\frac{3t^4}{12} = \\frac{(6 - 8 + 3)t^4}{12} = \\frac{t^4}{12} $$\n\nThe result matches option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
