    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the partial derivatives, we differentiate the vector $\\mathbf{a} = (u^2v, u + e^v, u + v^2)$ with respect to $u$ and $v$.\n1) $\\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{a}}{\\partial u} = (2uv, 1, 1)$.\n2) $\\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{a}}{\\partial v} = (u^2, e^v, 2v)$.\n3) $\\frac{\\partial^2 \\mathbf{a}}{\\partial u \\partial v} = \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}(2uv, 1, 1) = (2u, 0, 0)$.\n\nComparing these results with the options, Option H matches exactly: $(2uv, 1, 1)$, $(u^2, e^v, 2v)$, $(2u, 0, 0)$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
