    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10698",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let it be required to find the square roots of A where A = 3.08 + j8.455.\n\nOptions: \nA. 4∠35° and 4∠215°\nB. 2∠40° and 2∠220°\nC. 3.5∠45° and 3.5∠225°\nD. 2.8∠33° and 2.8∠213°\nE. 3∠45° and 3∠225°\nF. 3∠40° and 3∠220°\nG. 2.5∠30° and 2.5∠210°\nH. 3∠35° and 3∠215°\nI. 3∠30° and 3∠210°\nJ. 3∠50° and 3∠230°\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the square roots of $A = 3.08 + j8.455$, we first convert it to polar form. The magnitude is $|A| = \\sqrt{3.08^2 + 8.455^2} \\approx 9.0$ and the angle is $\\theta = \\arctan(8.455/3.08) \\approx 70^\\circ$. Thus, $A \\approx 9\\angle 70^\\circ$. The square roots are $\\pm\\sqrt{9}\\angle (70^\\circ/2)$, which gives $3\\angle 35^\\circ$ and $3\\angle (35^\\circ + 180^\\circ) = 3\\angle 215^\\circ$.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
