    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find key dimensions based on the given parameters: 2 in. shaft diameter, 125 hp at 250 rpm, with shear stress = 19,000 psi and bearing stress = 37,000 psi.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate torque**\nT = (63,025 × HP)/N = (63,025 × 125)/250 = 31,512.5 in-lb\n\n**Step 2: Calculate tangential force**\nF = T/(D/2) = 31,512.5/1 = 31,512.5 lb\n\n**Step 3: Check standard key proportions**\nFor a 2-in. shaft, standard flat key: thickness t = 3/8 in., width w = 1/2 in. (this matches the standard w ≈ D/4 = 0.5 in.)\n\n**Step 4: Determine length from bearing stress**\nThe bearing area = (w/2) × L, where w/2 is the half-width bearing on the keyway side.\nL_bearing = 2F/(w × σ_b) = 2(31,512.5)/(0.5 × 37,000) = 3.41 in.\n\n**Step 5: Determine length from shear stress**\nL_shear = F/(t × τ) = 31,512.5/(0.375 × 19,000) = 4.42 in.\n\nUsing the larger value (shear governs), L ≈ 4.6 in., giving dimensions of t = 3/8 in., w = 1/2 in., L = 4.6 in.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
