    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Five resistances of 10, 15, 20, 25, and 30 ohms are connected in parallel. Calculate the joint resistance.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.46 ohms\nB. 4.56 ohms\nC. 8.23 ohms\nD. 4.12 ohms\nE. 6.78 ohms\nF. 7.89 ohms\nG. 1.92 ohms\nH. 2.34 ohms\nI. 2.21 ohms\nJ. 5.67 ohms\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the joint resistance ($R_{eq}$) of resistors in parallel, use the formula $\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{R_n}$. Substituting the values: $\\frac{1}{R_{eq}} = \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{30} = 0.1 + 0.0667 + 0.05 + 0.04 + 0.0333 \\approx 0.29$. Thus, $R_{eq} \\approx \\frac{1}{0.29} \\approx 3.46$ ohms.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
