    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Methane reacts with water vapor at 25°C by the following reaction : CH_4(g) + H_2O(g) \\rightleftharpoons CO(g) + 3H_2(g) Using the following data, calculate the standard Gibbs free-energychange for this reaction. Data \\DeltaH_298^0(kcal mole^-1) \\DeltaS_298^0(cal deg^-1 mole^-1) CH_4(g) - 17.89 44.5 CO(g) - 26.40 47.3 H_2(g) 0 31.2 H_2O(g) - 57.80 45.1\n\nOptions: \nA. 34 kcal/mole\nB. 49,290 kcal/mole\nC. -10 kcal/mole\nD. 24.2 kcal/mole\nE. 60 kcal/mole\nF. 10,000 kcal/mole\nG. 15,280 kcal/mole\nH. 75.5 kcal/mole\nI. 51.3 kcal/mole\nJ. -20 kcal/mole\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the standard Gibbs free energy change ($\\Delta G^\\circ$), we first determine the enthalpy change ($\\Delta H^\\circ$) and entropy change ($\\Delta S^\\circ$) for the reaction. $\\Delta H^\\circ = [(-110.5) + 3(0)] - [(-74.8) + (-241.8)]$ kJ/mol is not directly applicable here as units are mixed; let's use the provided data in kcal and cal.\n$\\Delta H^\\circ_{rxn} = [\\Delta H_f^\\circ(CO) + 3\\Delta H_f^\\circ(H_2)] - [\\Delta H_f^\\circ(CH_4) + \\Delta H_f^\\circ(H_2O)] = [-26.40 + 0] - [-17.89 + (-57.80)] = -26.40 - (-75.69) = 49.29$ kcal/mol.\n$\\Delta S^\\circ_{rxn} = [\\Delta S^\\circ(CO) + 3\\Delta S^\\circ(H_2)] - [\\Delta S^\\circ(CH_4) + \\Delta S^\\circ(H_2O)] = [47.3 + 3(31.2)] - [44.5 + 45.1] = [47.3 + 93.6] - 89.6 = 140.9 - 89.6 = 51.3$ cal/(mol·K).\nAt $T = 298$ K, $\\Delta G^\\circ = \\Delta H^\\circ - T\\Delta S^\\circ$. Note that $\\Delta H^\\circ$ is in kcal and $\\Delta S^\\circ$ is in cal, so convert $\\Delta S^\\circ$ to kcal: $51.3 \\text{ cal/K} = 0.0513 \\text{ kcal/K}$.\n$\\Delta G^\\circ = 49.29 \\text{ kcal/mol} - (298 \\text{ K} \\times 0.0513 \\text{ kcal/(mol·K)}) = 49.29 - 15.2874 = 34.0026$ kcal/mol.\n\nThe calculated value is approximately 34 kcal/mole.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
