      "generated_answer": "Looking at this question, I need to identify which embryonic processes fail to fuse in complete bilateral cleft palate.\n\nIn normal palatogenesis, the **secondary palate** forms from the fusion of the **palatine (palatal) processes of the maxillary prominences** with each other and with the **primary palate** (derived from the frontonasal process). The secondary nasal processes are integral to the developing nose, and the maxillary processes give rise to the palatine processes that form the secondary palate.\n\nComplete bilateral cleft palate results from failure of the palatine processes to fuse with each other, with the primary palate (frontonasal process), and with tissues derived from the secondary nasal processes (which form the nasal septum/vomer region).\n\nThe answer is **C. palatine, frontonasal and secondary nasal processes.**\n\n\\boxed{C}",
