    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The probability of wrongly finding a difference when none exists is the Type I error rate ($\\alpha$), which is given as 1%. The probability of wrongly finding no difference when one exists is the Type II error rate ($\\beta$), which is given as 10%. Statistical power is defined as $1 - \\beta$, so the power is $1 - 0.10 = 0.90$ or 90%.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
