    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A teacher sets up a reward system for her elementary school students. At the end of each day, she gives a sticker to each student who showed up on time that morning. At the end of each week, she gives a sticker to any student who got above a 90% on three quizzes in a row. After months of this regimen, she finds that performance on the quizzes has increased significantly but that tardiness has only decreased slightly. Which of the following best explains the teacher’s observation?\n\nOptions: \nA. The students had more intrinsic motivation to do well on quizzes than to show up on time.\nB. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a variable-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nC. The students were more excited about the quizzes than about the reward system.\nD. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a variable-interval schedule than it was to a fixed-ratio schedule.\nE. Variable ratio schedules create the strongest responses and behavior that is the least susceptible to extinction.\nF. The students’ behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nG. The students' behavior change was weaker in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nH. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-interval schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nI. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a continuous reinforcement schedule than it was to a variable-ratio schedule.\nJ. The students’ behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a variable-interval schedule.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The daily sticker for being on time is a **continuous reinforcement schedule** (every instance of the desired behavior is rewarded). The weekly sticker for three consecutive quizzes above 90% is a **fixed-ratio schedule** (reward after a set number of desired behaviors).\n\nIn operant conditioning, continuous reinforcement typically produces faster initial learning but is more susceptible to extinction, while fixed-ratio schedules produce stronger, more persistent behavior change. The quiz performance (fixed-ratio) improved significantly more than the tardiness (continuous reinforcement), meaning the fixed-ratio schedule produced a stronger response.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
