    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "# Analysis of Congenital Diaphragmatic Hernia Prognostic Factors\n\nThe key prognostic factors in congenital diaphragmatic hernia (CDH) include pulmonary hypertension (major determinant of outcomes), size of the defect (larger defects correlate with worse outcomes and more lung hypoplasia), and gestational age at diagnosis (earlier diagnosis often indicates more severe disease with greater lung hypoplasia).\n\nDelay in emergent surgery is actually considered beneficial in modern CDH management, as delayed repair after cardiopulmonary stabilization has been shown to improve outcomes compared to emergency surgery. Current evidence supports avoiding urgent surgical repair in favor of stabilizing the patient first.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
