e options. A. yes, B. no, C. maybe. The text highlights that satisfaction was good in both groups (implied by \"Satisfaction levels... were good\" generally, and no other differences observed). If satisfaction is good, efficacy is likely perceived as sufficient. Therefore, the standard is reachable.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
