      "generated_answer": "\nThe study and meta-analysis consistently show that high Ki-67 expression is associated with poorer survival and disease progression in UTUC patients. The results from both the IHC analysis and the meta-analysis indicate that Ki-67 is an independent prognostic factor. Therefore, overexpression of Ki-67 is a prognostic biomarker of UTUC.  \n\nboxed{A}",
