    "prediction": "MiniMax-M3",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The L (Leading-tone exchange) transformation in Neo-Riemannian theory converts a major triad to a minor triad by moving the root down by a semitone. Applying L to A major (A-C#-E) moves the root A down to A#, resulting in A#-C#-E, which enharmonically respelled as B-C#-E is a C# minor triad, not A minor. \n\nLet me reconsider: The P (Parallel) transformation directly converts a major triad to its parallel minor by lowering the third by a semitone. A major (A-C#-E) becomes A minor (A-C-E) via the P transformation.\n\nThe answer is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
