    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at the original measure with L:1/8, we have `c3 z` in 2/4 time. The `c3` means three notes tied (dotted eighth + sixteenth), and `z` is a quarter rest (2 eighth-note durations).\n\nConverting to L:1/16: each original eighth becomes 2 sixteenths, so the quarter rest becomes 4 sixteenths.\n\nBreaking down `c3` (which was a dotted eighth + sixteenth = 1.5 eighth-note durations):\n- Dotted eighth = 3 sixteenths (`c3`)\n- Sixteenth = 2 sixteenths, but as a quarter of original eighth... \n\nThe standard breakdown is: `c3` → `c3-c3/2` (dotted eighth + sixteenth = 5 sixteenths representing 1.5 eighths), then we need the remaining sixteenth values to complete the measure (4 total sixteenths for the rest portion).\n\nOption B correctly shows: `c3-c3/2-c3/4 z/4 z/ z/4 z/4 z/ z` which properly subdivides the dotted notes and includes the rest values matching the 2/4 measure.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
