      "generated_answer": "Looking at this question about the Moche civilization, I need to identify what was built at the heart of their urban center, which was the city of Moche (also known as Cerro Blanco) on the north coast of Peru.\n\nThe Moche civilization (c. 100-700 CE) is famous for their monumental architecture centered around two massive structures: the Huaca del Sol (Temple/Pyramid of the Sun) and the Huaca de la Luna (Temple of the Moon). Their urban center was organized around these ceremonial platforms along with associated elite compounds and artisan workshops.\n\nAmong the given options, the most accurate answer is that the Moche built **an enormous walled-in precinct of elite residences** at the heart of their urban center. Archaeological excavations have revealed that the core of Moche city contained large walled compounds housing the elite ruling class, along with ceremonial platforms.\n\nThe other options can be ruled out: the Temple of the Feathered Serpent is associated with Teotihuacan, the Palace of the Painted Walls is not a Moche feature, the Pyramid of the Sun is Teotihuacan, the Moche had no writing system (eliminating libraries), and they did not have gladiatorial amphitheaters.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
